Subject: [PATCH 153/174] feat: LUT, ASC CDL and grade preset are CryEngine
 asset types (S10 item 4b, editor half)

The user's requirement: every grade-related file must be exportable, importable and
reusable, live under Assets, and be managed by cryassets. This is the half that makes
the files assets; the component half (pickers, presets) follows.

New Sandbox plugin Code/Sandbox/Plugins/CinematicCameraEditor -> one DLL in
EditorPlugins/. It registers three CAssetType subclasses and nothing else:

  CineLut   / .cube      colour LUTs - output transforms, looks, user LUTs
  CineCDL   / .cdl       ASC CDL (urn:ASC:CDL:v1.01)
  CineGrade / .cinegrade the whole CineCam Grade component in one file

All three are the CSoundType shape: IsImported false, no thumbnail, no editor window,
CanBeCreated false (a LUT is baked by tools/ocio-bake or exported from a grading
application; a preset is written by the component's own Export button). Registration
alone buys three things, which is why nothing else is needed:

  * the Asset Browser lists them, in the project AND under %engine%, because
    CAssetManager scans both roots;
  * a file copied into the project gets its .cryasset written for it, because
    CAssetGenerator registers a file-monitor listener per registered extension and RC's
    metadata compiler has a generic fallback for any extension it does not special-case;
  * every one of the three gets an Asset Browser resource selector named after its type,
    for free, from CAssetManager::RegisterAssetResourceSelectors - so no
    REGISTER_RESOURCE_SELECTOR is written anywhere.

A plugin rather than EditorQt/EditorCommon changes: deployment is one new file, the
shared editor binaries on S: stay untouched, and a stock editor without the DLL still
opens our levels (an unregistered selector name falls back to a text field).

Folder layout, replacing the ad-hoc Assets/ODT which stopped describing its contents two
items ago:

  Assets/cinecam/luts/          .cube, everything a person picks
  Assets/cinecam/luts/system/   .cube, machinery - the INVERSE output transform, an input
                                to the Rec.709 wrap that nobody ever selects. A separate
                                folder because a per-type picker cannot hide one file.
  Assets/cinecam/cdl/           .cdl
  Assets/cinecam/grades/        .cinegrade

Every shipped cube now carries a hand-written .cryasset in the same shape the project
already ships for ReC_Physical.env, so they are assets in a fresh install without the
editor, RC or a file watcher having to do anything.

Tools/CMake/BuildSandbox.cmake gains the add_subdirectory line (the plugin list is
hand-maintained; there is no glob).

Research: scene-notes/research/s10-4b-asset-system.md
Decisions: scene-notes/decisions/s10-grade-component.md section 4b.1 - 4b.3

